# No static service access

Runtime game code must receive dependencies through Zenject inject or constructor. Do not use static classes, `ProjectContext.Instance`, `TryResolve`, or `FindInOpenContainers` as a service locator.

```csharp
// BAD
DiContainer projectContainer = ProjectContext.Instance.Container;
T resolved = projectContainer.TryResolve<T>();

// BAD
public static class GameServices { public static IFoo Foo; }

// GOOD — field on a Mirror/MonoBehaviour object (ZenAutoInjecter SearchHierarchy)
[Inject]
private CharacterInputBuffer _input;

// GOOD — constructor on a bound service
public GameCameraService(GameCameraModel model, CameraCatalog catalog) { }
```

Network player prefabs use `ZenAutoInjecter` with `SearchHierarchy` so scene/Global bindings inject. Do not set `ContainerSources.ProjectContext`.

Allowed statics: `const` id/name holders (`CameraIds`, `SceneNames`), Unity `[MenuItem]` editor tools, and private static helpers that do not resolve services.
